responsive_hypotheses[6]:
  - scope: screen-ref01-app-shell
    hypothesis: "Sidebar and content widths are fixed logical widths, not percentages; the sidebar keeps a constant pixel width as the window widens."
    evidence: "Reference shell sidebar is 313px of 2048px; the settings reference keeps a 313px navigation at the same 2048px canvas, so the same absolute width appears at one canvas size only."
    confidence: 0.5
    validation_needed: Capture the native client at 1024/1280/1440/1920 widths and compare the sidebar's logical width in each.
  - scope: screen-ref01-app-shell
    hypothesis: The composer has a maximum width and stays centred in the visible content region rather than the full window.
    evidence: "Composer card measures 837px wide inside a 1734px content region, i.e. a fixed cap rather than a proportional fill."
    confidence: 0.6
    validation_needed: Capture the native client at three widths and compare composer width and centre offset.
  - scope: screen-ref06-settings
    hypothesis: The settings content column has a maximum width and is left-aligned inside the content region.
    evidence: "Column measures 874px inside a 1734px content region, leaving 717px of empty space on the right at this canvas size."
    confidence: 0.55
    validation_needed: Confirm at a wider canvas whether the column grows or stays capped.
  - scope: screen-ref04-sidebar
    hypothesis: "The sidebar crop is the same UI at a larger display scale, not a different density."
    evidence: "Row pitch is 36px in the shell reference and 62px in the sidebar crop, a ratio of about 1.7; both show the same row grammar."
    confidence: 0.55
    validation_needed: Identify the source scale of each capture before deriving any logical row height.
  - scope: screen-ref07-gather-office
    hypothesis: The office map is drawn at a single fixed tile grid with no zoom-dependent redraw of tiles.
    evidence: Corridor floor is one dominant near-uniform tone and props repeat at consistent scale across rooms in the same capture.
    confidence: 0.5
    validation_needed: Compare two captures at different office zoom levels and check whether tile edges stay crisp.
  - scope: screen-cur-office
    hypothesis: The current shell uses the same grid as the reference shell with different constants.
    evidence: Both capture a fixed-width sidebar plus a remaining-content region and a bottom-centred composer card.
    confidence: 0.7
    validation_needed: Compare the current client's captured logical rectangles at 1280x720 with the reference proportions.
uncertainties[12]:
  - property: font-family
    scope: "screen-ref01-app-shell, screen-ref03-effort-popover, screen-ref04-sidebar, screen-ref05-composer, screen-ref06-settings, screen-cur-office"
    reason: "No source metadata, design tokens or font binaries were supplied with any image; only ink heights and weights are measurable."
    confidence: 0.2
    recommended_validation: Read the native client's resolved font resource and its theme defaults; do not copy a reference product's typeface.
  - property: exact navigation row height and padding
    scope: screen-ref01-app-shell
    reason: "Row boxes were derived from measured ink bands and pitch, because the rows have no visible outline."
    confidence: 0.5
    recommended_validation: Read the running control's exported logical rectangle for one navigation row.
  - property: brand chip and footer avatar exact size
    scope: screen-ref01-app-shell
    reason: The pill-fill and luminance predicates returned loose boxes that include antialiasing and adjacent glyphs.
    confidence: 0.35
    recommended_validation: Re-measure from a 2x crop or read the native control's rect.
  - property: inspector panel bottom edge
    scope: screen-ref01-app-shell
    reason: "The scan window ended before the panel boundary, so only the top and left edges are measured."
    confidence: 0.4
    recommended_validation: "Re-scan the full panel column, or read the panel's rect at runtime."
  - property: selected navigation pill height
    scope: screen-ref06-settings
    reason: The fill predicate returned a 61px box that may include an adjacent highlighted row.
    confidence: 0.4
    recommended_validation: Re-measure with a tighter fill tolerance or read the control rect.
  - property: settings group and row boundaries
    scope: screen-ref06-settings
    reason: "Row heights vary with one- versus two-line descriptions, so a single uniform row height does not exist."
    confidence: 0.5
    recommended_validation: Read each row's exported logical rectangle in the settings view.
  - property: "chart, heatmap, donut, bar and segmented time-range controls"
    scope: "screen-cur-statistics-report, screen-cur-statistics-actions, screen-cur-quota"
    reason: "These elements are absent from the inspected captures; the newest statistics capture renders only text rows plus two chips and one button, and the quota capture renders no bars or legends."
    confidence: 0.75
    recommended_validation: "Confirm against the running client whether any chart surface exists; if it does not, the analytics cards must be built, not assumed."
  - property: duplicated explanatory note
    scope: "screen-cur-statistics-report, screen-cur-statistics-actions"
    reason: "The same sentence is drawn on two consecutive lines and the second begins mid-word, which indicates a wrap or duplicate-render defect rather than intentional copy."
    confidence: 0.7
    recommended_validation: Reproduce with a long note and inspect the label's wrap and container width.
  - property: office tile size and zoom mapping
    scope: "screen-ref07-gather-office, screen-cur-office"
    reason: "Colour autocorrelation over lags 10-120px on clean corridor patches returned a monotonically increasing difference with no local minimum in both the reference office and the current office, so no tile pitch could be resolved; props and shading also dominate the sampled patches."
    confidence: 0.3
    recommended_validation: Measure a clean empty floor patch in a fresh capture at known office zoom.
  - property: character sprite size and walk speed
    scope: screen-ref07-gather-office
    reason: Only one sprite is fully visible in the reference office; the measured 80x100 box includes its name pill.
    confidence: 0.4
    recommended_validation: Measure several sprites in a native capture at a known zoom.
  - property: provider usage card composition
    scope: screen-cur-quota
    reason: "The provider-usage reference was supplied as a parent description of an inline image that is not available to this session, so its composition is recorded as supplied-parent-description, not direct inspection."
    confidence: 0.3
    recommended_validation: "Re-inspect the original image directly, or read the runtime's actual spend and quota fields before building the card."
  - property: light-theme equivalents
    scope: all screens
    reason: "Every inspected reference and capture is a dark theme except the reported-problem render, which is light but is not a target design."
    confidence: 0.45
    recommended_validation: Capture the native client in its light theme at the same states before deriving light-theme tokens.
